# Crashing-bug utility check — did the 31-commit semantic overhaul hurt the
# crashing pipeline? 14 distinct KNOWN-crashing bugs (each seen crashing in
# past runs), balanced 7 overfit / 7 correct, spread across Chart/Lang/Math/
# Time and biased toward generic-JDK roots (parse SIOOBE/NFE, arithmetic) —
# the exact class the (now-gated) A2 attribution regression would have hit.
#
# This mirrors evaluate_crashing.sh: NO semantic flags (they are no-ops on
# crashing bugs anyway, now that bd9c8ab gates them). run.py auto-detects
# bug_kind=crashing. Decision rule: flagged overfitting <=> a harness still
# crashes the patched build.
#
# What to check in the results:
#   1. ZERO "[attribution]" lines in any run.log  (proves the crash-path gate
#      holds — a single line means A2 fired on a crashing bug = the regression).
#   2. overfit legs -> TP (still crashes patched); correct legs -> TN.
#   3. Per-bug outcomes consistent with history (crashing ran P0.90/R0.68/F1
#      0.78 across 45 mixed-version records); any overfit->FN or correct->FP
#      that contradicts history is a deep-dive target.
#
#   ./run_suite.sh crashcheck suites/crash14.cases
MODEL="gpt-5.4"
COMMON="-n 3 -m 20 --fuzz_timeout 30 --verify_timeout 30 --skip_semantic"
CASES=(
  "-o Lang 27 DeepRepair"
  "-o Lang 39 ACS"
  "-o Lang 45 Jaid"
  "-o Math 8 ssFix"
  "-o Math 49 Nopol2015"
  "-o Math 85 SimFix"
  "-o Math 97 ACS"
  "-c Chart 5 Arja"
  "-c Lang 6 SketchFix"
  "-c Lang 51 Jaid"
  "-c Lang 57 Elixir"
  "-c Math 4 ACS"
  "-c Math 70 Arja"
  "-c Time 7 SimFix"
)
